  <h2><strong>Determining Range and Maximum Height</strong></h2>

  <h4>1. Total flight time<br>
  <code>t<sub>D</sub></code></h4>
  <p>
    The horizontal range is
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: center;">
    <code>D = v<sub>0x</sub> · t<sub>D</sub></code>
  </p>
  <p>
    where <code>v<sub>0x</sub> = v<sub>0</sub> cos θ</code>.<br> The total flight time
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: center;">
    <code>t<sub>D</sub> = 2·t1 + t<sub>P</sub></code>
  </p>
  <p>
    – <strong>t1</strong> is the time to rise from <code>H0</code> to the apex (and the same time to descend back to <code>H0</code>),<br>
    – <strong>t<sub>P</sub></strong> is the time to fall from <code>H0</code> to the ground.
  </p>

  <h4>2. Ascent and descent to the same height</h4>
  <p>
    From vertical motion with initial upward speed <code>v<sub>0y</sub></code>:
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: center;">
    <code>0 = v<sub>0y</sub> − g·t₁  ⇒  t₁ = (v<sub>0y</sub>) / g</code>
  </p>

  <h4>3. Fall time from height <code>H0</code></h4>
  <p>
    Falling from <code>H0</code> with initial downward speed <code>v<sub>0y</sub></code> solves
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: center;">
    <code>½·g·t<sub>P</sub>² + v<sub>0y</sub>·t<sub>P</sub> − H₀ = 0</code>
  </p>
  <p>
    The positive root is:
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: center;">
    <code>t<sub>P</sub> = (−v<sub>0y</sub> + √<span class="kvadratni_koren">v<sub>0y</sub>² + 2·g·H0</span>) / g</code>
  </p>

  <h4>4. Final flight time</h4>
  <p>
    Substituting gives
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: center;">
    <pre><code>
      t<sub>D</sub> = 2·(v<sub>0y</sub>/g) + (−v<sub>0y</sub> + √<span class="kvadratni_koren">v<sub>0y</sub>² + 2·g·H0</span>)/g <br> 
      t<sub>D</sub>= (v<sub>0y</sub> + √<span class="kvadratni_koren">v<sub>0y</sub>² + 2·g·H0</span>) / g
    </code></pre>
  </p>

  <h4>5. Range</h4>
  <p style="text-align: center;">
    <strong>D = v<sub>0x</sub> · t<sub>D</sub></strong>
  </p>

  <h4>6. Maximum height above ground</h4>
  <p>
    The rise above <code>H0</code> is
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: center;">
    <pre>ΔH = (v<sub>0y</sub>²) / (2·g)</pre>
  </p>
  <p>
    Hence total maximum height:
  </p>
  <p style="text-align: center;">
    <strong>H<sub>max</sub> = H0 + (v<sub>0y</sub>²) / (2·g)</strong>
  </p>
</div>

